  receipts: [
    "**a Hugging Face repo folder read as the bytes it links to** (hf 1.33 keeps completed LFS files in a hub-level shared store, <cache_root>/blobs/<2 hex>/<sha256>, and leaves the repo folder's blobs/<hash> as a symlink into it, so a size, copy, mount or hard link of the repo folder that does not follow links reads or hands out pointers rather than bytes).",

    "INVALID STATE: a consumer sizing or exporting <cache_root>/models--<org>--<name> without dereferencing, or a hard link of a repo blob without -L. Before extdeps.huggingface.hub hub_cli_blob_store_layout, three consumers each re-encoded the fact as a bare `-L` with a prose comment (gunbc.spark.snapshot_rail_replica expose_one, gunbc.spark.group_checkpoint_materialize checkpoint_landed_on_host, gunbc.spark.group_arm_launch checkpoint_cache_bytes_lines), so a fourth consumer had nothing to import.",

    "HARM: during the GLM-5.3 fetch on srv7 2026-10-03 (read by valiant-crab-775) the repo folder SHRANK as files completed, which read as a fetch losing progress; a model-directory-only mount or a hard link of the symlink hands a dangling tree to the reader.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the repo blob is a symlink and its target lies under the cache root, outside the repo folder; only .incomplete partials are regular files in the repo folder.",

    "RUNG: found at 1. Now 2: the layout is a cited row in extdeps.huggingface.hub, the dereferencing argvs (hub_dereferenced_bytes_argv, hub_repo_blob_hard_link_argv) are derived from it, the three consumers route through them, and test.claim.huggingface.hub_blob_store_layout_witness_test reds when the row or the -L is removed. CEILING 3: a consumer could still spell its own `du`/`ln` argv over a hub path. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: hub cache paths carried as a typed path whose only byte-reading operations are the derived argvs, SUFFICIENT FOR no consumer to construct an undereferenced read of a repo folder.",
